<%# locals: (contest:, sim:, frames:)

    THE LAPTOP'S SIMULATED TOUCHDOWNS (Alex, 2026-10-06). The featured game in
    the live snapshot opens at LaptopScoreSimulation's 3-7, and every
    INTERVAL_MS a touchdown lands, drawn by /contests/<slug>/live's OWN
    machinery rather than a copy of it:

      contests/_live_script    the live page's script, unchanged, attached to
                               the snapshot's focus panel and strip by their
                               real wrapper ids (pages/_laptop_live)
      live/_score_banner       the banner it raises
      a hidden goal feed       the node a real score appends
      the showcase board       when the contest has no real entries
                               (LaptopShowcaseEntrants::Script), each frame's
                               board, re-ranked by the live script

    Each frame is what Contest::LiveBroadcast.goal_scored would send: the
    focus tile and strip chip at the new score, then the goal-feed node.
    LaptopLiveSnapshot#frames renders them server-side from the live page's
    partials, and the driver below swaps them in and appends the node, as Turbo
    does. The live script does the rest: the banner, the row wash, the
    touchdown sweep, the score pop, the hot score, the card's glow ring.
    "Touchdown +7" in the rail and the moving ball arrive with the tile.

    LOCAL ONLY. No cable subscription and no request: every frame is in the
    page. The leaderboard is never touched and keeps its real numbers.

    IT RUNS ONLY WHEN IT CAN BE SEEN: from xl (below it the laptop is not
    drawn), while the laptop is on screen, and while the tab is visible. Under
    prefers-reduced-motion it never starts, and the laptop holds the static
    opening frame; if reduced motion turns ON mid-visit (the media query is
    watched, not read once), it stops for good and puts the opening frame
    back. IT STOPS AT THE LAST FRAME (Alex, 2026-10-06): the touchdown that
    takes the combined score to LaptopScoreSimulation::STOP_AT (50) is held,
    with no loop back to 3-7, and the timer and every listener are cleared
    then, so nothing idles.

    IT LEAVES NOTHING BEHIND. Turbo keeps the document across a visit, so a
    listener on document, window or a media query outlives the page it was
    for, and retains it. Every one of them is removed on turbo:visit,
    turbo:before-render and pagehide (not a bfcache one), whether the timer is
    running or paused; before this a paused laptop leaked one set per visit.

    STATE FOR THE TESTS, on the sim root: data-sim is "reduced" (never
    started), "paused", "running", "done" (held on the last frame) or
    "stopped"; data-armed is set the first
    time a timer is armed and never cleared; data-frame is the frame last
    drawn. window.__laptopSimLive counts drivers wired and not yet torn
    down (0 or 1 on a healthy page). %>
<%# The live script's goal feed. The two holds are shortened from the live
    page's 50s and 45s so a score cools before the next one lands. %>
<div id="contest_<%= contest.id %>_goal_feed" class="hidden" aria-hidden="true"
     data-hot-ms="8000" data-glow-ms="8000"></div>
<div hidden data-test="laptop-sim"
     data-game-slug="<%= sim.source.slug %>"
     data-interval-ms="<%= LaptopScoreSimulation::INTERVAL_MS %>"
     data-contest-id="<%= contest.id %>"
     data-opening="<%= sim.opening.game.away_score %>-<%= sim.opening.game.home_score %>">
  <%# Frames 1..TOUCHDOWNS. Frame 0, the opening 3-7, is the snapshot itself;
      the driver copies it on load, to put back if reduced motion turns on. %>
  <% frames.each do |frame| %>
    <template data-frame="<%= frame[:index] %>" data-part="tile"><%= frame[:tile].html_safe %></template>
    <template data-frame="<%= frame[:index] %>" data-part="chip"><%= frame[:chip].html_safe %></template>
    <template data-frame="<%= frame[:index] %>" data-part="feed"><%= frame[:feed].html_safe %></template>
    <% if frame[:board] %>
      <template data-frame="<%= frame[:index] %>" data-part="board"><%= frame[:board].html_safe %></template>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
</div>
<%= render "live/score_banner" %>
<%= render "contests/live_script", contest: contest %>
<script>
  (function () {
    var root = document.querySelector('[data-test="laptop-sim"]');
    if (!root || root.dataset.wired) return;   // once per page, across Turbo visits
    root.dataset.wired = '1';

    var motion = window.matchMedia && window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)');
    if (motion && motion.matches) { root.dataset.sim = 'reduced'; return; } // the static opening frame

    var id      = root.dataset.contestId;
    var slug    = root.dataset.gameSlug;
    var every   = Number(root.dataset.intervalMs) || 10000;
    var feed    = document.getElementById('contest_' + id + '_goal_feed');
    var focus   = document.getElementById('contest_' + id + '_focus');
    var games   = document.getElementById('contest_' + id + '_games');
    // Present only for the scripted showcase board (pages/_laptop_live).
    var board   = document.getElementById('contest_' + id + '_leaderboard');
    var laptop  = root.closest('[data-test="laptop-mock"]') || root;
    var wide    = window.matchMedia('(min-width: 1280px)');
    var tileAt  = '[data-test="live-focus-game"][data-focus-slug="' + slug + '"]';
    var chipAt  = '[data-test="live-game-chip"][data-game-slug="' + slug + '"]';
    var count   = root.querySelectorAll('template[data-part="tile"]').length + 1;
    if (!feed || !focus || count < 2) return;

    // FRAME 0 IS THE PAGE AS IT LOADED: copies of the opening tile and chip,
    // taken before anything moves, put back if reduced motion turns on.
    var opening = {
      tile: focus.querySelector(tileAt) && focus.querySelector(tileAt).cloneNode(true),
      chip: games && games.querySelector(chipAt) && games.querySelector(chipAt).cloneNode(true),
      board: board ? board.innerHTML : null
    };

    var index = 0, timer = null, onScreen = false, observer = null, live = true;
    window.__laptopSimLive = (window.__laptopSimLive || 0) + 1;

    function part(i, name) {
      if (i === 0) return opening[name] || null;
      var t = root.querySelector('template[data-frame="' + i + '"][data-part="' + name + '"]');
      return t ? t.content.firstElementChild : null;
    }

    function swap(container, selector, fresh) {
      if (!container || !fresh) return;
      Array.prototype.forEach.call(container.querySelectorAll(selector), function (node) {
        node.replaceWith(fresh.cloneNode(true));
      });
    }

    // The panel first, then the announcement: the live script lights the
    // scoring row on the next animation frame, so it finds the new score.
    function show(i) {
      swap(focus, tileAt, part(i, 'tile'));
      swap(games, chipAt, part(i, 'chip'));
      // THE SHOWCASE BOARD, when there is one: replaced whole, as a broadcast
      // updates the live board, so the live script re-ranks it (the slide, the
      // wash, the rank badge, the score pop).
      if (board) {
        var next = i === 0 ? opening.board
                 : (root.querySelector('template[data-frame="' + i + '"][data-part="board"]') || {}).innerHTML;
        if (next != null) board.innerHTML = next;
      }
      var node = part(i, 'feed');
      if (node) feed.appendChild(node.cloneNode(true));
      root.dataset.frame = String(i);
    }

    function step() {
      if (!root.isConnected) return stop(true);  // Turbo left the page
      index += 1;
      show(index);
      // The last frame is the cap: hold it, clear the timer, drop the listeners.
      if (index >= count - 1) { stop(true); root.dataset.sim = 'done'; }
    }

    function running() {
      return root.isConnected && wide.matches && onScreen && document.visibilityState === 'visible';
    }
    function sync() {
      if (!live) return;
      if (running()) {
        if (!timer) { timer = setInterval(step, every); root.dataset.armed = '1'; }
        root.dataset.sim = 'running';
      } else {
        if (timer) { clearInterval(timer); timer = null; }
        root.dataset.sim = 'paused';
      }
    }
    // Detach removes EVERY listener this driver added, paused or not.
    function stop(detach) {
      if (timer) { clearInterval(timer); timer = null; }
      if (detach && live) {
        live = false;
        root.dataset.sim = 'stopped';
        window.__laptopSimLive = Math.max(0, (window.__laptopSimLive || 1) - 1);
        document.removeEventListener('visibilitychange', sync);
        if (wide.removeEventListener) wide.removeEventListener('change', sync);
        if (motion && motion.removeEventListener) motion.removeEventListener('change', onMotion);
        document.removeEventListener('turbo:visit', leave);
        document.removeEventListener('turbo:before-render', leave);
        window.removeEventListener('pagehide', onPageHide);
        if (observer) observer.disconnect();
      }
    }
    function leave() { stop(true); }
    function onPageHide(event) { if (!event.persisted) stop(true); }
    // Reduced motion switched on mid-visit: stop, and hold the opening frame.
    function onMotion(event) {
      if (!event.matches) return;
      stop(true);
      index = 0;
      show(0);
    }

    root.dataset.sim = 'paused';
    document.addEventListener('visibilitychange', sync);
    if (wide.addEventListener) wide.addEventListener('change', sync);
    if (motion && motion.addEventListener) motion.addEventListener('change', onMotion);
    document.addEventListener('turbo:visit', leave);
    document.addEventListener('turbo:before-render', leave);
    window.addEventListener('pagehide', onPageHide);
    if ('IntersectionObserver' in window) {
      observer = new IntersectionObserver(function (entries) {
        onScreen = entries.some(function (e) { return e.isIntersecting; });
        sync();
      });
      observer.observe(laptop);
    } else {
      onScreen = true;
      sync();
    }
  })();
</script>
